{
  "id": "africa",
  "title": "Africa: peoples, cities and kingdoms",
  "period": "about 300,000 years ago to 1495 CE · overview, then rewind",
  "area": "africa",
  "intro": "A continental tour before the close-up. Each stop is a selected dated moment, not a claim about a whole kingdom’s duration. The last five views change geographic scale, then the story rewinds to Nok.",
  "method": "Points locate sites or city centres with stated uncertainty, never empire outlines. Architecture is an original symbolic schematic, not a scale reconstruction or an emblem. Geography and the river locator are generalised modern physical references, not ancient coastlines, riverbanks or lake extents. Capital identifications and dates remain qualified. The tour explicitly jumps and rewinds; its progress rail shows scene order, not proportional years.",
